# Step 1. Retrieve the human LEP protein sequence
  1. Open UniProt: https://www.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/P41159/entry
  2. Search for P41159.
  3. Open the protein entry.
  4. Locate the FASTA sequence.
  5. Download the FASTA file.

# Step 2. Download the AlphaFold structure
  1. Open the AlphaFold database entry for P41159: https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/entry/P41159
  2. Locate the 3D protein structure.
  3. Download the structure in PDB format if available, or mmCIF if that is the offered format.
  4. Save it as: human_LEP_AlphaFold.pdb

# Step 3. Install and open PyMOL
Refer to the Software_Requirements.txt file for download instructions.
  1. After installation, open PYMOL.
  2. Locate the downloaded human_LEP_AlphaFold.pdb file.
  Load it using the command line:
load human_LEP_AlphaFold.pdb, lep_full
  If your downloaded file is in another folder, provide its full file path.
  For example, on Windows:
load C:/Users/YourName/Downloads/human_LEP_AlphaFold.pdb, lep_full
  You should now see your leptin protein structure.

# Step 4. Visualize the full-length LEP structure
  Enter these commands one at a time:
hide everything
show cartoon, lep_full
color cyan, lep_full
bg_color white
orient lep_full

# Step 5. Remove the signal peptide to obtain mature LEP
select mature_LEP, lep_full and resi 22-167

create lep_mature, mature_LEP

hide everything
show cartoon, lep_mature

color marine, lep_mature

orient lep_mature

# Step 5.1 Check the residue count:
count_atoms lep_mature and name CA

# Step 6. Examine the secondary structure
hide everything
show cartoon, lep_mature

dss lep_mature

color gray80, lep_mature
color red, lep_mature and ss H
color yellow, lep_mature and ss S
color green, lep_mature and ss L

orient lep_mature

# Step 7. Visualize AlphaFold confidence scores
hide everything
show cartoon, lep_full

spectrum b, red_yellow_green, lep_full, minimum=50, maximum=100

orient lep_full

# Step 8. Save your mature LEP structure and PYMOL session
save human_LEP_mature.pdb, lep_mature

save human_LEP_analysis.pse

# Step 9. Generate a high-resolution image of the protein structure
bg_color white
set ray_opaque_background, off
ray 2000, 2000
png human_LEP_structure.png, dpi=300
